@OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5019

###

# Authenticate in Development with the dev key (set it with `dotnet user-secrets` or the .env file; never commit it).
@devApiKey = {{$processEnv DEV_API_KEY}}

### Any protected endpoint accepts the key in X-Api-Key (production uses a JWT bearer token instead)
GET {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/health
X-Api-Key: {{devApiKey}}

### Route an order: canonical v1 path (valid; 201 Created with the routing envelope, the stored `id` and a Location header, using the seeded reference data)
POST {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/route
X-Api-Key: {{devApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order_id": "ORD-EXAMPLE",
  "customer_zip": "10015",
  "mail_order": false,
  "items": [
    { "product_code": "WC-STD-001", "quantity": 1 },
    { "product_code": "OX-PORT-024", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Route an order: alias of v1, pinned to v1 (same handler, same contract)
POST {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/api/route
X-Api-Key: {{devApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "order_id": "ORD-EXAMPLE",
  "customer_zip": "10015",
  "mail_order": false,
  "items": [ { "product_code": "WC-STD-001", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

### Get a stored order (OR-028): paste the `id` from the POST response above. 200 with the stored request and the same decision; 404 for an unknown id, a non-UUID id or another caller's order
GET {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/route/0193a1b2-7c3d-7e4f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b
X-Api-Key: {{devApiKey}}

### Invalid request: 400 with every error in the v1 envelope (missing customer_zip, empty items)
POST {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/route
X-Api-Key: {{devApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "order_id": "ORD-BAD", "items": [] }

### Malformed JSON: 400 in the same envelope
POST {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/route
X-Api-Key: {{devApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ not json

### No credentials: 401 with WWW-Authenticate, nothing is validated
POST {{OrderRouter_Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/route
Content-Type: application/json

{ "order_id": "ORD-BAD", "items": [] }
